@startuml fig_history_vs_current
!include _style.puml
' Book figure — current state only vs retained history.
' Form: structure. Evidence status: conceptual illustration; asserts no rate.
title undoing the state is not the same as erasing the evidence
top to bottom direction
skinparam nodesep 18
skinparam ranksep 28

rectangle "1 . current state only" as PA #FBFBF6 {
  rectangle "Donation\nstatus = PAID" as A1 <<authoritative>>
  rectangle "refund applied\nstatus = REFUNDED" as A2 <<authoritative>>
  A1 --> A2 : overwrite
}
note bottom of A2
  After the refund the PAID state is gone.
  "Was this ever paid?" is now unanswerable.
end note

rectangle "2 . retained history" as PB #FBFBF6 {
  rectangle "DonationEvent\n(event_id, donation_id,\nevent_type, occurred_at)" as B1 <<authoritative>>
}
note bottom of B1
  PLEDGED -> PAID -> REFUNDED are appended.
  The same question is answered: undo the state,
  keep the evidence.
end note

A2 -[hidden]right-> B1
@enduml
